dent' activity at some point later in the same process instance. Conversely, a 'Document Incident' event can occur only if a 'Close Incident' event has occurred before it within the same process instance. This bidirectional and ordered dependency ensures that 'Close Incident' impose obligations for future 'Document Incident', and 'Document Incident' cannot occur without prior 'Close Incident'. Multiple 'Close Incident' and 'Document Incident' are allowed, with each 'Close Incident' eventually leading to a 'Document Incident' and each 'Document Incident' being justified by a preceding 'Close Incident'.\",\"template\":\"Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Close Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Close Incident' activity involves closing the incident after resolution and verification.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Document Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Document Incident' activity involves documenting all details related to the incident.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"unary\",\"description\":\"The 'Escalate Incident' must not occur 2 times in the process.\",\"template\":\"Absence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Escalate Incident\",\"description\":\"The 'Escalate Incident' activity involves escalating the incident to a higher level of authority.\"},\"target\":null,\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":2}]}"